  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "0ada9836-12e6-41ff-bb4e-fb8914aaebe8",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -8016,
        5808
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1136,
        "height": 1008,
        "content": "## AI Terraform PR Review & Security Agent\n\n### How it works\n1. A GitHub pull request touching Terraform files triggers the workflow.\n2. An AI agent decides which checks to run — a plan diff, a security scan, a cost estimate, and a search of internal IaC standards.\n3. It writes a structured review with a pass/fail verdict per category and an overall risk rating.\n4. The review is posted back to the PR as a comment and logged to Postgres for audit history.\n5. Clean reviews auto-approve the PR; anything flagged high-risk routes to a human via Slack before it can merge.\n\n### Setup\n- [ ] Add GitHub credentials (repo scope, PR write access) on the trigger and all GitHub nodes\n- [ ] Add an OpenAI credential and a Vector Store credential for the RAG tool\n- [ ] Wire Tool - Run Terraform Plan and Tool - Run Security Scan to your CI runner — never let the agent apply, only plan/scan\n- [ ] Wire Tool - Estimate Cost Impact to Infracost's API or CLI output\n- [ ] Add a Postgres credential and create the `terraform_pr_reviews` table\n- [ ] Add Slack credentials on the security-review notification node\n- [ ] Point Wait - For Security Sign-Off's resume webhook at your reviewer UI's approve/request-changes action\n\n### Customization\nOpen a test PR touching a .tf file to run end-to-end, then push again to the same PR to confirm the sessionId keeps review context across revisions."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "04603ed9-0366-48c3-8892-cf97d4283d9d",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Trigger & Review Agent",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -6512,
        5712
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 1552,
        "height": 1152,
        "content": "## Trigger and review\n\nFetches the PR's Terraform diff, then has an AI agent call whichever tools it needs — plan, security scan, cost estimate, IaC standards search — before writing a structured review."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "cb13888c-ba29-4c81-a733-05fb77de1806",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Logging & Auto-Gate",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -4880,
        5696
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 928,
        "height": 944,
        "content": "## Log and post the review\n\nSaves the structured review for audit history, posts it as a PR comment, then checks whether it's clean enough to auto-approve."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "bb6a41b1-9126-426b-bbc2-cfcb392c7c55",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Human Security Gate & Merge",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -3920,
        5696
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 1264,
        "height": 944,
        "content": "## Approve or escalate to security\n\nAuto-approves clean PRs; flagged ones wait on a human security sign-off in Slack before merging or requesting changes."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
